1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:09,010
The last stanza is the only one that asks for something concrete, and what it asks for is simply more time: O let us see another day!

2
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:12,486
The exclamation mark is the loudest sound in the poem.

3
00:00:12,486 --> 00:00:19,518
Then the whole town, in his imagination, bows to the setting sun and says good-bye, but just for now.

